# Handles: the small numbers a program holds for the host's objects (buffers, maps, sets; files and
# listings in stage 3), numbered from 1 and never reused, so a handle used after it was closed or
# after its region was released traps naming its kind, as `refined run` does. A region lists the
# handles it owns and closes them when it is released.
#
# This module is generated from tools/handles.dsl by tools/build.py.
